---
title: Mapo Tofu (麻婆豆腐)
description: A famous Sichuan tofu dish that is spicy, numbing, hot, aromatic and tender.
prep time: 15 minutes
cook time: 15 minutes
servings: 4
tags:
  - tofu
  - chinese
  - sichuan
course: Main
---

== Preparation ==

Cut @silken tofu{400%g} into cubes. Blanch in boiling @water{} with a pinch of @salt{} for ~{2%minutes}. Carefully remove and drain.

Minced @pork or beef{150%g}.

Chop @garlic{3%cloves}, @ginger{1%tbsp}, and @scallions{2}.

== Cooking ==

Heat @oil{2%tbsp} in a #wok{} over medium heat. Fry @Sichuan peppercorns{1%tsp} until fragrant, then remove the peppercorns and keep the flavored oil.

Add the minced meat and stir-fry until browned and crispy.

Add @doubanjiang{2%tbsp} (spicy broad bean paste) and @fermented black beans{1%tbsp} (douchi), and fry until the oil turns red and fragrant.

Add the chopped garlic and ginger, and stir-fry for ~{1%minute}.

Pour in @chicken stock or water{1%cup}, @light soy sauce{1%tbsp}, and @sugar{1/2%tsp}. Bring to a simmer.

Carefully slide in the blanched tofu. Simmer over low heat for ~{5%minutes} to let the tofu absorb the flavors.

== Finishing ==

Mix @cornstarch{1%tbsp} with @water{2%tbsp} to create a slurry. Drizzle it into the wok in three batches, stirring gently by pushing the back of your spatula against the bottom of the wok to avoid breaking the tofu.

Turn off the heat, drizzle with @sesame oil{1%tsp}.

Transfer to a serving dish, sprinkle with chopped scallions and @ground roasted Sichuan peppercorn powder{1/2%tsp}.
